I am bad with English so i will go short.
If you love action that involves a lot of some RPG elements - in this case items and some skills for awesome action;
And if you like nice electronic music and one of such artists is Sonic Mayhem [Sascha Dikiciyan] who made classic game music for games Quake II and Quake III Arena [plus lots more including Tron game and Warhammer];
And if you like crazy humor that adds to game flawor huge positive energy;
And if you like unusual art style;
And if you like fantastic experience in co-op mode with your friends - THIS IS THE GAME YOU SHOULD GO FOR!
And really - you should have this game. It is long time since i had such a nice adrenalin rush playing game and basically being in euphoria from its music.
10 out of 10.

Undertale. Looks like it belongs on the NES or SNES,doesn't it? Something tells me that's part of the plan from Toby Fox,the leading mind behind the game. Due to the intricate nature of Undertale's plot,it's impossible to talk at length about it without spoiling something,so,I'll just say this;
Play the game. It's worth every penny. It's a refreshing take on RPG as a genre,and storytelling as a whole. And as you play,remember things. Never stop thinking. And if you get a hunch? Act on it. If you've somehow managed to avoid spoilers about the game,then this game's a treat. Play it as blind as you can,and Undertale will take you for a wild ride that you'll be hard-pressed to forget.
And the soundtrack is absolutely PHENOMENAL. I'd kill for a Mettaton-themed rhythm game.

